[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3458166716","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112007#issuecomment-3458166716","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112007","id":3458166716,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7OH2-8","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-28T19:33:12Z","updated_at":"2025-10-28T19:34:54Z","body":"The PhysicsServer is set to be inactive in the editor, so this must be due to something else (AnimationPlayer/AnimationTree being active while in the editor).\n\nPS: You may be able to get the issue to happen faster by using `--time-scale 100` when opening the editor, or by setting `Engine.time_scale = 100` in a `@tool` script. If you do this, I also recommend increasing **Physics > Common > Max Physics Steps per Frame** to `100` in the Project Settings to avoid slowdown.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3458166716/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3992576118","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112007#issuecomment-3992576118","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112007","id":3992576118,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7t-eB2","user":{"login":"Sauroniux","id":69519260,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5NTE5MjYw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69519260?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauroniux","html_url":"https://github.com/Sauroniux","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauroniux/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauroniux/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauroniux/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauroniux/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauroniux/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauroniux/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauroniux/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauroniux/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauroniux/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-03T17:37:59Z","updated_at":"2026-03-03T17:37:59Z","body":"I tried to take a look at this bug and this what I found:\n\n1. `PhysicalBoneSimulator3D::_process_modification` is being called every frame\n2. Because the simulation is not running, it calls `PhysicalBone3D::reset_to_rest_position`\n3. That then results in a `Node3D::set_global_transform` call which adds the `PhysicalBone3D` to the dirty transform list  \n4. While processing the transform change notification, `PhysicalBone3D` calls `PhysicalBone3D::update_offset` which recomputes the offset with a tiny float error. That error later gets added to the global transform of the `PhysicalBone3D` node.\n6. The cycle continues indefinitely\n\nSo this results in a recursion where the offset is based on the transform but the transform is based on the offset. Maybe it would make sense to stop computing the offset from the transform, and make it only be driven by the offset property itself? Like the `SpringBoneCollision*3D` nodes do when they are attached to a bone. Which I guess would be a breaking change.\n\nI tried changing the offset calculation to increase accuracy, but my attempts were not enough for a perfect float round-trip.\n\nI think this is also the same issue as in #59577.\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3992576118/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4420688567","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112007#issuecomment-4420688567","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112007","id":4420688567,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABB35atw","user":{"login":"PiCode9560","id":122909224,"node_id":"U_kgDOB1NyKA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/122909224?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PiCode9560","html_url":"https://github.com/PiCode9560","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PiCode9560/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PiCode9560/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PiCode9560/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PiCode9560/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PiCode9560/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PiCode9560/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PiCode9560/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PiCode9560/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PiCode9560/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-11T12:30:28Z","updated_at":"2026-05-11T12:30:28Z","body":"> So this results in a recursion where the offset is based on the transform but the transform is based on the offset. Maybe it would make sense to stop computing the offset from the transform, and make it only be driven by the offset property itself? Like the `SpringBoneCollision*3D` nodes do when they are attached to a bone. Which I guess would be a breaking change.\n\nI was looking into #103206 and it seems like stopping offset computation from the transform also fixed it. I think it's a decent solution.\n\nAs a bonus this change will make the physical bone behaviour consistent to the spring bone collision.\n\nI believe that it is not really a breaking changes since it only changed the editor workflow, and not modifying any API.\n\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4420688567/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4420978827","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112007#issuecomment-4420978827","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112007","id":4420978827,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABB4LIiw","user":{"login":"PiCode9560","id":122909224,"node_id":"U_kgDOB1NyKA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/122909224?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PiCode9560","html_url":"https://github.com/PiCode9560","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PiCode9560/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PiCode9560/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PiCode9560/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PiCode9560/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PiCode9560/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PiCode9560/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PiCode9560/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PiCode9560/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PiCode9560/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-11T13:08:34Z","updated_at":"2026-05-11T13:08:34Z","body":"To make `body_offset` easier to edit, we could provide `body_position_offset` and `body_rotation_offset` like the `SpringBoneCollision*3D`\n\n<img width=\"612\" height=\"167\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/53c76a71-46ca-4480-b569-f8159328cc40\" />\n\n\nOr alternatively, we could also just add an option to edit `Transform3D` as position and rotation (and scale).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4420978827/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]